### ampersand followed by a semicolon
./server --port 8080 &; echo "server started"
>>- SC1045 1:23 -- bash rejects &; so this is a parser syntax error whose message says to drop the ;

### ampersand separating two commands
./server --port 8080 & echo "server started"
>>> none

### backgrounded command ending a case branch
case $1 in
  serve) ./server &;;
esac
>>> none
